<urn:kg:ofev:pisection:8e50ecd9-a631-4459-ae17-a792631abd5c> a kg:PISection ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT <urn:kg:ofev:document:c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c> ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_SECTION <urn:kg:ofev:section:8e50ecd9-a631-4459-ae17-a792631abd5c> ;
    kg:PI_SECTION_CONTAINS_SAFETY <urn:kg:ofev:safety:8e50ecd9-a631-4459-ae17-a792631abd5c> ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 12 ;
    kg:section_id "8e50ecd9-a631-4459-ae17-a792631abd5c" ;
    kg:section_title "Risk Summary" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text "There is no information on the presence of nintedanib in human milk, the effects on the breast-fed infant or the effects on milk production. Nintedanib and/or its metabolites are present in the milk of lactating rats [see Data] . Because of the potential for serious adverse reactions in nursing infants from OFEV, advise women that breastfeeding is not recommended during treatment with OFEV." .

<urn:kg:ofev:pisection:9145a320-c5e0-4d9e-92e5-60e0f39171ef> a kg:PISection ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT <urn:kg:ofev:document:c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c> ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_SECTION <urn:kg:ofev:section:9145a320-c5e0-4d9e-92e5-60e0f39171ef> ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 29 ;
    kg:section_id "9145a320-c5e0-4d9e-92e5-60e0f39171ef" ;
    kg:section_title "16 HOW SUPPLIED/STORAGE AND HANDLING" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text """150 mg:  brown, opaque, oblong, soft capsules imprinted in black with the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol and "150". They are packaged in HDPE bottles with a child-resistant closure, available as follows: Bottles of 60 NDC:  0597-0145-60

100 mg:  peach, opaque, oblong, soft capsules imprinted in black with the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol and "100". They are packaged in HDPE bottles with a child-resistant closure, available as follows: Bottles of 60                                        NDC:  0597-0143-60""" .

<urn:kg:ofev:pisection:91983fed-49c3-48ad-bcce-8a2ee884137a> a kg:PISection ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT <urn:kg:ofev:document:c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c> ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_SECTION <urn:kg:ofev:section:91983fed-49c3-48ad-bcce-8a2ee884137a> ;
    kg:PI_SECTION_CONTAINS_SAFETY <urn:kg:ofev:safety:91983fed-49c3-48ad-bcce-8a2ee884137a> ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 5 ;
    kg:section_id "91983fed-49c3-48ad-bcce-8a2ee884137a" ;
    kg:section_title "Nausea and Vomiting" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text "In IPF studies (Study 1, Study 2, and Study 3), nausea was reported in 24% versus 7% and vomiting was reported in 12% versus 3% of patients treated with OFEV and placebo, respectively. In the chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype study (Study 5), nausea was reported in 29% versus 9% and vomiting was reported in 18% versus 5% of patients treated with OFEV and placebo, respectively. In the SSc-ILD study (Study 4), nausea was reported in 32% versus 14% and vomiting was reported in 25% versus 10% of patients treated with OFEV and placebo, respectively [see Adverse Reactions (6.1)] . In most patients, these events were of mild to moderate intensity. In IPF studies (Study 1, Study 2, and Study 3), nausea led to discontinuation of OFEV in 2% of patients and vomiting led to discontinuation of OFEV in 1% of the patients. In the chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype study (Study 5), nausea led to discontinuation of OFEV in less than 1% of patients and vomiting led to discontinuation of OFEV in 1% of the patients. In the SSc-ILD study (Study 4), nausea led to discontinuation of OFEV in 2% of patients and vomiting led to discontinuation of OFEV in 1% of the patients." .

