<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:12a94596-9118-4578-bde0-af999466a4d1> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "12a94596-9118-4578-bde0-af999466a4d1" ;
    kg:chunk_index 44 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 6 ;
    kg:section_id "a4673fef-9d6d-461c-8ebd-800465280c8c" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "b1545a005491b33def830b52c79170e3ba65a91d2516d1ae89372ff060f1e5c8" ;
    kg:text "For nausea or vomiting that persists despite appropriate supportive care including anti-emetic therapy, dose reduction or treatment interruption may be required [see Dosage and Administration (2.4)] . OFEV treatment may be resumed at the full dosage (150 mg twice daily), or at the reduced dosage (100 mg twice daily), which subsequently may be increased to the full dosage. If severe nausea or vomiting does not resolve, discontinue treatment with OFEV." ;
    kg:token_count 114 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:14d49f95-98b4-4064-8a21-a34d6f9bf1ff> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "14d49f95-98b4-4064-8a21-a34d6f9bf1ff" ;
    kg:chunk_index 131 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 25 ;
    kg:section_id "6ad4dd31-dcd4-4ea0-bc69-54a13057e025" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "afd2e5af8b18f7b6cb845efe6e7b73765c1c6229e5862f7950b14503b40692fe" ;
    kg:text """Acute ILD exacerbation was defined as unexplained worsening or development of dyspnea within 30 days, new diffuse pulmonary infiltrates on chest x-ray, and/or new HRCT parenchymal abnormalities with no pneumothorax or pleural effusion, and exclusion of alternative causes. Acute ILD exacerbations were not adjudicated.

The risk of first acute ILD exacerbation did not show a statistically significant difference between the OFEV group compared to placebo (52 week treatment period: HR 0.72, (95% CI: 0.38, 1.37); whole trial: HR 0.63 (95% CI: 0.37, 1.07)).""" ;
    kg:token_count 139 .

