<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:39d35ebc-1412-49a6-9966-3ae2245925c5> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "39d35ebc-1412-49a6-9966-3ae2245925c5" ;
    kg:chunk_index 118 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 42 ;
    kg:section_id "f6ac55d4-b4ca-4a20-b5dd-9c93c1cf6592" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "bd3b7debedc5a345f582ead1af9e0772ba5d75a0adb366772f5edffb400dbc48" ;
    kg:text "The campaign headline speaks directly to changing the decline in lung function to slow disease progression in IPF. It also serves as a strong call to action for HCPs. For too long, HCPs have felt helpless but now they have the power to change lives with OFEV ® , a long-awaited treatment for IPF." ;
    kg:token_count 74 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:3a9270c9-2b52-42a5-b803-525a2d94801a> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "3a9270c9-2b52-42a5-b803-525a2d94801a" ;
    kg:chunk_index 41 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 5 ;
    kg:section_id "4af45440-1a4c-40e7-89c6-c4fe9171b8f4" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "47a2c73c42c41b0626ceed1c198934db35b620236a5b53cc17e978138b545abd" ;
    kg:text """atients. In the SScILD study (Study 4), diarrhea was reported in 76% versus 32% of patients treated with OFEV and placebo, respectively [see Adverse Reactions (6.1)]. Diarrhea led to permanent dose reduction in 22% of patients treated with OFEV compared to 1% of placebo-treated patients. Diarrhea led to discontinuation of OFEV in 7% of the patients compared to 0.3% of placebo-treated patients.

Dosage modifications or treatment interruptions may be necessary in patients with adverse reactions of diarrhea. Treat diarrhea at first signs with adequate hydration and antidiarrheal medication (e.g., loperamide), and consider dose reduction or treatment interruption if diarrhea continues [see Dosage and Administration (2.4)]. OFEV treatment may be resumed at the full dosage (150 mg twice daily), or at the reduced dosage (100 mg twice daily), which subsequently may be increased to the full dosage. If severe diarrhea persists despite symptomatic treatment, discontinue treatment with OFEV.""" ;
    kg:token_count 248 .

