<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:52db56bf-9745-4c06-b7ad-78530b39b786> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "52db56bf-9745-4c06-b7ad-78530b39b786" ;
    kg:chunk_index 71 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 11 ;
    kg:section_id "e132de83-5540-40ac-8205-fbf673f5350b" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "02bbfa4b859f79430686730d79f6c948e73f41346a2c55504d27f38b4f80e34a" ;
    kg:text "In a multiple-dose study conducted to assess the pharmacokinetic effects of concomitant treatment with nintedanib and pirfenidone, the coadministration of nintedanib with pirfenidone did not alter the exposure of either agent [see Clinical Pharmacology (12.3)] . Therefore, no dose adjustment is necessary during concomitant administration of nintedanib with pirfenidone." ;
    kg:token_count 93 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:52f20d07-3dfa-4e30-bce1-05dbdec35151> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "52f20d07-3dfa-4e30-bce1-05dbdec35151" ;
    kg:chunk_index 90 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 14 ;
    kg:section_id "2f4aa101-da41-4ebc-af80-9fc0275c10e7" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "90f739f001427f320afe4fadcfb4f1076b9bf79137f47157c57b238232aa5cc9" ;
    kg:text """Its structural formula is:

<!-- image -->

Nintedanib esylate is a bright yellow powder with an empirical formula of C31H33N5O4·C2H6O3S and a molecular weight of 649.76 g/mol.

OFEV capsules for oral administration are available in 2 dose strengths containing 100 mg or 150 mg of nintedanib (equivalent to 120.40 mg or 180.60 mg nintedanib ethanesulfonate, respectively). The inactive ingredients of OFEV are the following: Fill Material: triglycerides, hard fat, lecithin. Capsule Shell: gelatin, glycerol, titanium dioxide, red ferric oxide, yellow ferric oxide, black ink.""" ;
    kg:token_count 144 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:53479369-4351-4bb5-a333-ee2f4861c168> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "53479369-4351-4bb5-a333-ee2f4861c168" ;
    kg:chunk_index 80 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 12 ;
    kg:section_id "8210acc5-e3a6-43f3-9aee-9ddffde6eadc" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "d393dc2438671c5daa86c47a3e0767cc9a3166f208d191c9ed01e9464f704e2b" ;
    kg:text "OFEV can cause fetal harm when administered to a pregnant woman. Advise females of reproductive potential to avoid becoming pregnant while receiving treatment with OFEV. Advise females of reproductive potential to use highly effective contraception at initiation of, during treatment, and for at least 3 months after taking the last dose of OFEV. Nintedanib does not change the exposure to oral contraceptive containing ethinylestradiol and levonorgestrel in patients with SSc-ILD. However, the efficacy of oral hormonal contraceptives may be compromised by vomiting and/or diarrhea or other conditions where the drug absorption may be reduced. Advise women taking oral hormonal contraceptives experiencing these conditions to use alternative highly effective contraception." ;
    kg:token_count 194 .

