<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:7350b932-2ae3-4e96-842e-8157ddb56815> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "7350b932-2ae3-4e96-842e-8157ddb56815" ;
    kg:chunk_index 162 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 31 ;
    kg:section_id "d155d159-cf19-4a92-99b6-baf15353036b" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "430f7ca41e2f80d4da65b62cb5dc991d871fbdad30db527966d8dcfb9da14e34" ;
    kg:text """- See 'What is the most important information I should know about OFEV?'
- liver problems. Call your doctor right away if you have unexplained symptoms such as yellowing of your skin or the white part of your eyes (jaundice), dark or brown (tea colored) urine, pain on the upper right side of your stomach area (abdomen), bleeding or bruising more easily than normal, feeling tired, or loss of appetite. Your doctor will do blood tests to check how well your liver is working before starting and during your treatment with OFEV.
- diarrhea, nausea, and vomiting. While you are taking OFEV, your doctor may recommend that you drink fluids or take medicine to treat these side effects. Tell your doctor if you have diarrhea, nausea, or vomiting or if these""" ;
    kg:token_count 188 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:73a6d5b5-26ba-4276-b1b4-7f36c7767d89> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "73a6d5b5-26ba-4276-b1b4-7f36c7767d89" ;
    kg:chunk_index 2 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 1 ;
    kg:section_id "6e058b55-c461-46b2-b07a-9d99ebc88ec7" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "89bc040395952464851024cf267d4a444f03d612915487065a4814f37de58321" ;
    kg:text """- Recommended dosage: 150 mg taken orally twice daily approximately 12 hours apart taken with food. (2.2)
- Recommended dosage in patients with mild hepatic impairment (Child Pugh A): 100 mg taken orally twice daily approximately 12 hours apart taken with food. (2.3, 8.6)
- Consider temporary dose reduction to 100 mg, treatment interruption, or discontinuation for management of adverse reactions. (2.4, 5.2, 5.3, 6)
- Prior to treatment initiation, conduct liver function tests in all patients and a pregnancy test in females of reproductive potential. (2.1, 5.2, 5.4)""" ;
    kg:token_count 143 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:740f8c75-33b4-4699-9f5f-765ad09d67cf> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "740f8c75-33b4-4699-9f5f-765ad09d67cf" ;
    kg:chunk_index 98 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 15 ;
    kg:section_id "4f7f8f81-109a-4044-b44a-092bbfbe27d6" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "15047bd545866d6828e55ff5977faba8c8909988ecca6449c6ca4475b250c2d4" ;
    kg:text "The major route of elimination of drug-related radioactivity after oral administration of [ 14 C] nintedanib was via fecal/biliary excretion (93.4% of dose), and the majority of OFEV was excreted as BIBF 1202. The contribution of renal excretion to the total clearance was low (0.65% of dose). The overall recovery was considered complete (above 90%) within 4 days after dosing." ;
    kg:token_count 94 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:744166f0-37e1-45ab-8068-09885063c733> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "ofev-epar-medicines-overview_en.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "744166f0-37e1-45ab-8068-09885063c733" ;
    kg:chunk_index 7 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 2 ;
    kg:section_id "8725de24-48b7-4c09-8ba2-7d1eefd322aa" ;
    kg:source_document_id "dcf1cfdd-57dc-4936-b9b2-0839e9684cb2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "product_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "ofev-epar-medicines-overview_en.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "626de81ba9ab027f9fbac8e64634e3391ee82f123b58f14e9e65fa626809c0cc" ;
    kg:text "The European Medicines Agency decided that Ofev's benefits are greater than its risks and it can be authorised for use in the EU. The Agency considered that Ofev is effective at slowing down the worsening of lung function in adult patients with IPF, systemic sclerosis-associated ILD and other chronic fibrosing ILDs that are progressive." ;
    kg:token_count 84 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:74446ddf-2949-45b9-ae11-b419c9d70d4f> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "74446ddf-2949-45b9-ae11-b419c9d70d4f" ;
    kg:chunk_index 70 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 11 ;
    kg:section_id "16b697b1-2d28-41a6-9698-b87c9099fcec" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "87c9a2521530903bf77a4c2562db950375e2c8ed5b407a16f4304ee942fc188f" ;
    kg:text "Nintedanib is a VEGFR inhibitor and may increase the risk of bleeding. Monitor patients on full anticoagulation therapy closely for bleeding and adjust anticoagulation treatment as necessary [see Warnings and Precautions (5.6)]." ;
    kg:token_count 57 .

