    kg:source_hash "62217f862eb8f99f2e797e96510167985adb41216fa36bbad3682ad090374d31" ;
    kg:text """Our clinical trial logo consists of 2 elements: the trial name and the symbol. The symbol depicts a hummingbird, representing vigor and energy. The dark blue, all-caps typeface in the trial name communicates innovation and intelligence.

<!-- image -->

triAL nAME""" ;
    kg:token_count 66 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:9024b902-c7ff-456e-a0b4-7334a9c18b02> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "9024b902-c7ff-456e-a0b4-7334a9c18b02" ;
    kg:chunk_index 49 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 6 ;
    kg:section_id "f94298fb-422a-4154-b6cd-b1226caaa6eb" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "a9f13b86f2da5c7d030a99e2394056883b250a40be24334b673558006fefdc9c" ;
    kg:text """Based on the mechanism of action (VEGFR inhibition), OFEV may increase the risk of bleeding. In IPF studies (Study 1, Study 2, and Study 3), bleeding events were reported in 10% of patients treated with OFEV and in 7% of patients treated with placebo. In the chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype study (Study 5), bleeding events were reported in 11% of patients treated with OFEV and in 13% of patients treated with placebo. In the SSc-ILD study (Study 4), bleeding events were reported in 11% of patients treated with OFEV and in 8% of patients treated with placebo. In clinical trials, epistaxis was the most frequent bleeding event reported.

In the postmarketing period non-serious and serious bleeding events, some of which were fatal, have been observed.

Use OFEV in patients with known risk of bleeding only if the anticipated benefit outweighs the potential risk.""" ;
    kg:token_count 222 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:9124e088-3eec-4b99-9ca6-fcac4a8e926f> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "9124e088-3eec-4b99-9ca6-fcac4a8e926f" ;
    kg:chunk_index 55 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 7 ;
    kg:section_id "3e128188-269d-498c-a537-2a7ef88f114d" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "67628c746d379468396995519e6923a10ad4838ce743347211a5f74e0af627f9" ;
    kg:text """iPF is devastating and unpredictable. Physicians are powerless, and patients live in fear.

the progressive loss of lung function erodes life and results in death by suffocation within 2-3 years of diagnosis.

While most patients experience gradually declining lung function, some also experience precipitous, commonly fatal drops known as acute exacerbations. these come without warning or known cause, and have a direct effect on accelerating disease progression.""" ;
    kg:token_count 116 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:91898a45-98bc-4602-a186-58a7e9ff3ff0> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "91898a45-98bc-4602-a186-58a7e9ff3ff0" ;
    kg:chunk_index 149 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 29 ;
    kg:section_id "c86d5e52-8881-44d3-808e-eeab92a27e40" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "221bd7a702d9f813b9b77640ac253911198969f3e66cbac05be9b7681dda8bd7" ;
    kg:text "Advise patients about the signs and symptoms of acute myocardial ischemia and other arterial thromboembolic events and the urgency to seek immediate medical care for these conditions [see Warnings and Precautions (5.5)]." ;
    kg:token_count 55 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:9215c1b0-e31f-4d23-af1e-51fd5b82d44e> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "9215c1b0-e31f-4d23-af1e-51fd5b82d44e" ;
    kg:chunk_index 123 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 22 ;
    kg:section_id "ce5bae28-2e04-4264-918e-5980b4dd50a7" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "7429d60078294f297b09e67da648195ed6497deb318e04bd503b5d94198e7d96" ;
    kg:text "The majority of patients were Caucasian (74%) or Asian (25%). Patients were mostly male (54%) and had a mean age of 66 years and a mean FVC percent predicted of 69%, and 49% were never-smokers. The underlying clinical ILD diagnoses in groups represented in the trial were hypersensitivity pneumonitis (26%), autoimmune ILDs (26%), idiopathic nonspecific interstitial pneumonia (19%), unclassifiable idiopathic interstitial pneumonia (17%), and other ILDs (12%)." ;
    kg:token_count 115 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:923b6ae3-d9c7-4097-965c-d6169fdeb01e> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "923b6ae3-d9c7-4097-965c-d6169fdeb01e" ;
    kg:chunk_index 111 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 17 ;
    kg:section_id "ebb892d5-08b1-49bf-b307-e908ca83a34f" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "752c22700047d2b4c3df647264381391e74676bd5ad0a6458e1b9b1e7e9a705b" ;
    kg:text "weeks of entry into this trial, or n-acetyl cysteine and prednisone (greater than 15 mg/day or equivalent) within 2 weeks. The majority of patients were Caucasian (60%) or Asian (30%) and male (79%). Patients had a mean age of 67 years and a mean FVC percent predicted of 80%." ;
    kg:token_count 69 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:92a5d3fd-9710-4116-bade-2f5854c2a3c4> a kg:Chunk ;
