    kg:source_hash "1d4b9b078a950bf1bcf65a9acdb7dca44d006b2b4ed1bdfffd2f0083cc84ac79" ;
    kg:text """In the event that there is a need to use a different patient type or activity level within the context of this background imagery, new photography can be retouched into the existing backgrounds. Here are some general guidelines for photography if this need arises.

1.  Studio: Talent may be photographed against a plain, white, seamless background
2. Camera: Use a medium format camera with an 80 mm lens
3. Camera position: Set camera 12 to 13 feet from subject, approximately at height of subject's waist
4. Lighting: To match lighting conditions of the backgrounds, use a hard light high up on camera left to emulate sunlight and a fill light lower on camera right

