    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "a679d3d16b600eae9d74c37fb014ef53f217b1cb798a89daf0dfe5ec52f0710c" ;
    kg:text "Verify the pregnancy status of females of reproductive potential prior to treatment with OFEV and during treatment as appropriate [see Dosage and Administration (2.1), Warnings and Precautions (5.4), and Use in Specific Populations (8.1)]." ;
    kg:token_count 60 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:b8fd6ff0-a9a9-44aa-ab2c-052e40e004f3> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "b8fd6ff0-a9a9-44aa-ab2c-052e40e004f3" ;
    kg:chunk_index 54 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 7 ;
    kg:section_id "d2d3fed3-3838-425a-af8a-118326fe3ab8" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "d7799174ee0d2c54456310e96d1bc37126e8996cff043efb6aefd94fce56f8f7" ;
    kg:text """Because clinical trials are conducted under widely varying conditions, adverse reaction rates observed in the clinical trials of a drug cannot be directly compared to rates in the clinical trials of another drug and may not reflect the rates observed in practice.

The safety of OFEV was evaluated in over 1000 IPF patients, 332 patients with chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype, and over 280 patients with SSc-ILD. Over 200 IPF patients were exposed to OFEV for more than 2 years in clinical trials.""" ;
    kg:token_count 129 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:b97af278-7722-400a-a960-f3e25a4d9250> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "b97af278-7722-400a-a960-f3e25a4d9250" ;
    kg:chunk_index 151 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 59 ;
    kg:section_id "d8624806-6eb4-4b24-a32f-1fa592abb4ac" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "ca47d898cc8072b7283a1c196a4da8aa4cbe61a6ae7fb2b2412c6a25952cace2" ;
    kg:text """The HCP unbranded identity system comprises key assets that are designed, managed, and used in a recognizable way across all of our disease state communication materials.

Our identity system unifies our unbranded materials in a consistent, flexible, and ownable way across all channels, allowing us to communicate consistently to the HCP community.""" ;
    kg:token_count 87 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:ba6eac01-9b7b-4e49-a153-b129edbfa52a> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "ba6eac01-9b7b-4e49-a153-b129edbfa52a" ;
    kg:chunk_index 50 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 7 ;
    kg:section_id "72235e47-f19c-4d6d-9129-d75e2319f70d" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "96643822fca791e7a9d2bbb4dcd4510342be9a86b49c27776cc1cfdf50b427ff" ;
    kg:text """Based on the mechanism of action, OFEV may increase the risk of gastrointestinal perforation. In IPF studies (Study 1, Study 2, and Study 3), gastrointestinal perforation was reported in less than 1% of patients treated with OFEV, compared to 0 cases in the placebo-treated patients. In the chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype study (Study 5), gastrointestinal perforation was not reported in any patients in any treatment arm. In the SSc-ILD study (Study 4), no cases of gastrointestinal perforation were reported in patients treated with OFEV or in placebo-treated patients.

In the postmarketing period, cases of gastrointestinal perforations have been reported, some of which were fatal.

Use caution when treating patients who have had recent abdominal surgery, previous history of diverticular disease or receiving concomitant corticosteroids or NSAIDs. Discontinue therapy with OFEV in patients who develop gastrointestinal perforation. Only use OFEV in patients with known risk of gastrointestinal perforation if the anticipated benefit outweighs the potential risk.""" ;
    kg:token_count 272 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:ba92e54c-7913-4d09-bba2-629b53080f4f> a kg:Chunk ;
