    kg:section_id "b6c67302-a0f0-4c66-aa02-059141f00da2" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "9b42315fdaabaf57a1986647c176f584da61b7dc46056f038bf469c896af155c" ;
    kg:text """A secondary graphic is a brand element that symbolizes our personality and unifies our brand across all communications. Our secondary graphic is a combination of two geometric shapes: the Guardian Blue shape that appears on the bottom of the page, and the golden gradient shape that appears on the top of the page. Together, these two shapes create a space that represents the change OFEV ®  is creating in the path of IPF.

The two shapes that make up our secondary graphic should appear together on every communication piece. The Guardian Blue shape should never appear on a page without the golden gradient shape and vice versa.

Our secondary graphic has been provided in both a vertical and a horizontal format for flexibility of use (see next page).

<!-- image -->""" ;
    kg:token_count 193 .

