<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:cbc212ea-e6ed-48c7-bd7a-19252dd56e26> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "ofev-epar-medicines-overview_en.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "cbc212ea-e6ed-48c7-bd7a-19252dd56e26" ;
    kg:chunk_index 6 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 2 ;
    kg:section_id "305d4f42-378d-478d-aaa3-ac9d5c838b6a" ;
    kg:source_document_id "dcf1cfdd-57dc-4936-b9b2-0839e9684cb2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "product_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "ofev-epar-medicines-overview_en.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "16a8749bee455688719c223d95142d28edd4684175b9ef616395b697bba31c15" ;
    kg:text """For the full list of side effects and restrictions with Ofev, see the package leaflet.

The most common side effects with Ofev (which may affect more than 1 in 10 people) include diarrhoea, nausea (feeling sick), vomiting, abdominal pain (belly ache), decreased appetite and raised levels of liver enzymes in the blood (a sign of liver problems). Weight loss (which may affect up to 1 in 10 people) is also common.

Ofev must not be used in patients who are hypersensitive (allergic) to nintedanib, peanut or soya, or any of the other ingredients. Ofev must also not be used in pregnant women.""" ;
    kg:token_count 148 .

<urn:kg:ofev:chunk:cbc9ff30-1ef2-4eaa-8fab-78e776609966> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
