<urn:kg:ofev:section:214eca65-ca27-49f0-af14-a8dc20079943> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:8be15576-14fd-40ea-a499-a3e27e31eb87> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 84 ;
    kg:section_id "214eca65-ca27-49f0-af14-a8dc20079943" ;
    kg:section_title "Typography" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:text """The primary font selected for the clinical trial branding is Chalet. Progressive and scientific, Chalet complements the logo well; it is also the font in which the trial names are set. The secondary font used for body copy is Helvetica Neue Roman.

<!-- image -->

Aa Headlines should be Chalet-London Nineteen Seventy sentence case SUBHEADS SHOULD BE CHALET-NEW YORK NINETEEN SEVENTY

Body copy should be Helvetica Neue Roman sentence case in 80%K. Body call-outs should be in Helvetica Neue Bold.

Call-outs should be Chalet-London Nineteen Seventy sentence case""" .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:2201299c-0fe7-4cb4-9e0e-09f8886e8639> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:3e5da516-4da8-4d7d-9182-e9c4a8887680>,
        <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:4197e007-57b5-48db-b01e-72d9ab8d20c8> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 32 ;
    kg:section_id "2201299c-0fe7-4cb4-9e0e-09f8886e8639" ;
    kg:section_type "body" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text """symptoms do not go away or become worse. Tell your doctor if you are taking over-the-counter laxatives, stool softeners, and other medicines or dietary supplements that can cause diarrhea.

- heart attack. Tell your doctor right away if you have symptoms of a heart problem. These symptoms may include chest pain or pressure, pain in your arms, back, neck or jaw, or shortness of breath.
- stroke. Tell your doctor right away if you have symptoms of a stroke. These symptoms may include numbness or weakness on 1 side of your body, trouble talking, headache, or dizziness.
- bleeding problems. OFEV may increase your chances of having bleeding problems. Tell your doctor if you have unusual bleeding, bruising, or wounds that do not heal. Tell your doctor if you are taking a blood thinner, including prescription blood thinners and over-the-counter aspirin.
- tear in your stomach or intestinal wall (perforation). OFEV may increase your chances of having a tear in your stomach or intestinal wall. Tell your doctor if you have pain or swelling in your stomach area.
- increased protein in your urine (proteinuria). OFEV may increase your chances of having protein in your urine. Tell your doctor if you have any signs and symptoms of protein in the urine such as foamy urine, swelling, including in your hands, arms, legs, or feet, or sudden weight gain.

The most common side effects of OFEV are diarrhea, nausea, stomach pain, vomiting, liver problems, decreased appetite, headache, weight loss, and high blood pressure.

These are not all the possible side effects of OFEV. For more information, ask your doctor or pharmacist. Call your doctor for medical advice about side effects. You may report side effects to FDA at 1-800-FDA-1088.""" .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:235a46e9-9ff0-4617-af28-670c8536daaa> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:fbb64338-3a7f-4127-8f7e-568826261c69> ;
