<urn:kg:ofev:section:8210acc5-e3a6-43f3-9aee-9ddffde6eadc> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:53479369-4351-4bb5-a333-ee2f4861c168> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 12 ;
    kg:section_id "8210acc5-e3a6-43f3-9aee-9ddffde6eadc" ;
    kg:section_title "Contraception" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text "OFEV can cause fetal harm when administered to a pregnant woman. Advise females of reproductive potential to avoid becoming pregnant while receiving treatment with OFEV. Advise females of reproductive potential to use highly effective contraception at initiation of, during treatment, and for at least 3 months after taking the last dose of OFEV. Nintedanib does not change the exposure to oral contraceptive containing ethinylestradiol and levonorgestrel in patients with SSc-ILD. However, the efficacy of oral hormonal contraceptives may be compromised by vomiting and/or diarrhea or other conditions where the drug absorption may be reduced. Advise women taking oral hormonal contraceptives experiencing these conditions to use alternative highly effective contraception." .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:82a26947-5b97-41bb-a052-8ef1dcf57a12> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:b2f76536-feb1-4c57-b7a8-56cced026375> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 98 ;
    kg:section_id "82a26947-5b97-41bb-a052-8ef1dcf57a12" ;
    kg:section_title "Clinical T rial Logo Nomenclature" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:text """The following nomenclature system has been developed to help identify and easily locate the various graphic files. Please always use the downloadable electronic reproducible art we have provided.

The various file formats available are: AI (Adobe Illustrator) files are used for all high-quality printing. These files are in a vector format and can be scaled up or down without loss of quality.

JPG (Joint Photographic Experts Group) files are in a compressed format best used on the Internet because they are in RGB. They cannot be scaled up without loss of quality.

PNG (Portable Network Graphics) files are used for importing artwork into PowerPoint for on-screen presentations. These files can also be used on the Internet. This is a compressed format; files are best created at full size and not scaled up or down. PNG files are created with a transparent background.""" .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:8725de24-48b7-4c09-8ba2-7d1eefd322aa> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "ofev-epar-medicines-overview_en.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:744166f0-37e1-45ab-8068-09885063c733> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 2 ;
    kg:section_id "8725de24-48b7-4c09-8ba2-7d1eefd322aa" ;
    kg:section_title "Why is Ofev authorised in the EU?" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "dcf1cfdd-57dc-4936-b9b2-0839e9684cb2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "product_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "ofev-epar-medicines-overview_en.pdf" ;
    kg:text "The European Medicines Agency decided that Ofev's benefits are greater than its risks and it can be authorised for use in the EU. The Agency considered that Ofev is effective at slowing down the worsening of lung function in adult patients with IPF, systemic sclerosis-associated ILD and other chronic fibrosing ILDs that are progressive." .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:872fc0cc-8d81-4568-9f2b-277ffba4e222> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
