    kg:text "13.1  Carcinogenesis, Mutagenesis, Impairment of Fertility" .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:89202da0-0ccd-4f15-acee-1666d4e198de> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:35b24151-9162-49fa-8cd6-34add4bf74fc> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 95 ;
    kg:section_id "89202da0-0ccd-4f15-acee-1666d4e198de" ;
    kg:section_title "Logo File Nomenclature" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:text """The following nomenclature system has been developed to help identify and easily locate the various graphic files. Please always use the downloadable electronic reproducible art we have provided.

The various file formats available are: AI (Adobe Illustrator) files are used for all high-quality printing. These files are in a vector format and can be scaled up or down without loss of quality.

JPG (Joint Photographic Experts Group) files are in a compressed format best used on the Internet because they are in RGB. They cannot be scaled up without loss of quality.

PNG (Portable Network Graphics) files are used for importing artwork into PowerPoint for on-screen presentations. These files can also be used on the Internet. This is a compressed format; files are best created at full size and not scaled up or down. PNG files are created with a transparent background.""" .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:8c93e117-6515-4c2d-9dcf-2cfcba6f6bd2> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:86506077-f95b-429a-a25d-16c9ad995fde> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 50 ;
    kg:section_id "8c93e117-6515-4c2d-9dcf-2cfcba6f6bd2" ;
    kg:section_title "Color Palette" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:text """The OFEV ®  colors were selected to reinforce our brand identity and to differentiate our brand from competitors. They should be used to help maintain brand recognition and impact. The OFEV ®  core brand color is Guardian Blue, and it should be the most prominent color in the palette. In addition, Guardian Blue is the only color that should be used with the line pattern.

The three secondary colors, Inspiring Yellow, Brilliant Gold, and Premium Orange, reflect the colors used in the OFEV ®  gradient. Premium Orange may be used for highlights in applications as well as in typographical call-outs and subheads.

Comfort Gray is included as a neutral tertiary color that helps balance the palette. Comfort Gray can be used in clinical and scientific situations, such as in charts or to represent placebo.

<!-- image -->""" .

