<urn:kg:ofev:section:a4673fef-9d6d-461c-8ebd-800465280c8c> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:12a94596-9118-4578-bde0-af999466a4d1> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 6 ;
    kg:section_id "a4673fef-9d6d-461c-8ebd-800465280c8c" ;
    kg:section_type "body" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text "For nausea or vomiting that persists despite appropriate supportive care including anti-emetic therapy, dose reduction or treatment interruption may be required [see Dosage and Administration (2.4)] . OFEV treatment may be resumed at the full dosage (150 mg twice daily), or at the reduced dosage (100 mg twice daily), which subsequently may be increased to the full dosage. If severe nausea or vomiting does not resolve, discontinue treatment with OFEV." .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:aba56e41-f812-4087-864d-9b80c5b0eaf8> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:bd820940-f6f3-41cb-b2d6-94d1c93fb8f2> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 64 ;
    kg:section_id "aba56e41-f812-4087-864d-9b80c5b0eaf8" ;
    kg:section_title "Campaign Visual" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:text """The campaign visual works to clearly communicate the unstable and unpredictable nature of IPF. The visual features a man walking on ice that is beginning to crack behind him. The ice symbolizes the uncertain and harsh landscape of IPF, while the cracks in the ice represent the unpredictable and severe outcomes for patients with IPF.

The campaign is flexible and can be utilized across all unbranded communications. The artwork is able to accommodate large areas and can also be cropped around the man walking on ice when needed. However, it is advised that the cracks of ice not be cropped too much so that the impact of the visual is not lost.

The campaign headline should always accompany the visual (see 6.6 for headline).

Additional artwork is available for the sheet of ice without the patient or ice cracks. This can be used when the full campaign is not needed.

<!-- image -->

ExAMPLES oF cAMPAiGn ViSuAL in ProMotionAL MAtEriALS

<!-- image -->

<!-- image -->

icE SHEEt ArtWorK

<!-- image -->""" .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:ac548616-122c-4ca0-a4c3-01eb83b4a49a> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:e8cc6b6b-9ccd-40ce-8f78-568952d99462> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 69 ;
    kg:section_id "ac548616-122c-4ca0-a4c3-01eb83b4a49a" ;
    kg:section_title "Patient Unbranded Identity System 7.0" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:text """The patient unbranded identity system comprises key assets that are designed, managed, and used in all of our disease education communication materials.

Our identity system unifies our unbranded materials in a consistent, flexible, and ownable way across all channels, allowing us to communicate consistently to the IPF patient community.""" .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:aedd0ddd-2309-405b-9b27-36237e738956> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:accaf163-7520-4085-be27-448ee29fe1ce> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 40 ;
    kg:section_id "aedd0ddd-2309-405b-9b27-36237e738956" ;
    kg:section_title "Direction for conducting localised green screen photoshoot" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:text """In the event that there is a need to use a different patient type or activity level within the context of this background imagery, new photography can be retouched into the existing backgrounds. Here are some general guidelines for photography if this need arises.

1.  Studio: Talent may be photographed against a plain, white, seamless background
2. Camera: Use a medium format camera with an 80 mm lens
3. Camera position: Set camera 12 to 13 feet from subject, approximately at height of subject's waist
4. Lighting: To match lighting conditions of the backgrounds, use a hard light high up on camera left to emulate sunlight and a fill light lower on camera right

<!-- image -->

