    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:text """Typography is another important element of our brand identity and a way to express our personality. The OFEV ®  primary fonts are Co Text Bold and Co Text Light. Co Text complements the visual elements seen in the OFEV ®  symbol and is also the font that the OFEV ®  logotype is based on. The OFEV ®  secondary font, used for body copy, is the Gotham Family, including Gotham Book, Gotham Bold, and Gotham Italic.

<!-- image -->

aa""" .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:d8624806-6eb4-4b24-a32f-1fa592abb4ac> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:b97af278-7722-400a-a960-f3e25a4d9250> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 59 ;
    kg:section_id "d8624806-6eb4-4b24-a32f-1fa592abb4ac" ;
    kg:section_title "hcP unbranded Identity System 6.0" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:text """The HCP unbranded identity system comprises key assets that are designed, managed, and used in a recognizable way across all of our disease state communication materials.

Our identity system unifies our unbranded materials in a consistent, flexible, and ownable way across all channels, allowing us to communicate consistently to the HCP community.""" .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:d89b2866-1a7e-4aa3-b16e-387715043740> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:e8a52d2d-8491-4b3f-ab5c-8ce44f6b45b5> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 41 ;
    kg:section_id "d89b2866-1a7e-4aa3-b16e-387715043740" ;
    kg:section_title "Patient Imagery" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
    kg:text """The patients depicted in the existing campaign have been photographed in a neutral setting to provide additional flexibility and utility throughout multiple communication platforms.

<!-- image -->""" .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:d98137e4-1182-40a9-a960-56289cab694d> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:32a50cc3-f02b-4b7f-9734-60f6a70030de> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 25 ;
    kg:section_id "d98137e4-1182-40a9-a960-56289cab694d" ;
    kg:section_title "Survival" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text "Survival was evaluated for OFEV compared to placebo in Study 5 to support the primary endpoint (FVC). Allcause mortality was assessed over the study duration and available follow-up period, irrespective of cause of death and whether patients continued treatment. All-cause mortality did not show a statistically significant difference (52 week treatment period: HR 0.94 (95% CI: 0.47, 1.86); whole trial: HR 0.78 (95% CI: 0.50, 1.21))." .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:da5d26bb-3aa5-4f5b-8be4-78fb6851cc6a> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
