<urn:kg:ofev:section:c86d5e52-8881-44d3-808e-eeab92a27e40> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:91898a45-98bc-4602-a186-58a7e9ff3ff0> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 29 ;
    kg:section_id "c86d5e52-8881-44d3-808e-eeab92a27e40" ;
    kg:section_title "Arterial Thromboembolic Events" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text "Advise patients about the signs and symptoms of acute myocardial ischemia and other arterial thromboembolic events and the urgency to seek immediate medical care for these conditions [see Warnings and Precautions (5.5)]." .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:cb34e383-a4e4-405d-9df0-348aeeed7701> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "ofev-epar-medicines-overview_en.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:63596c76-dcbc-44f1-899a-754eed9b302f> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 3 ;
    kg:section_id "cb34e383-a4e4-405d-9df0-348aeeed7701" ;
    kg:section_type "body" ;
    kg:source_document_id "dcf1cfdd-57dc-4936-b9b2-0839e9684cb2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "product_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "ofev-epar-medicines-overview_en.pdf" ;
    kg:text """Based on the disease characteristics and how the medicine works, the medicine's effectiveness for treating clinically significant progressive fibrosing ILD and systemic sclerosis-associated ILD in children is expected to be similar as in adults. However, long-term safety data for children are not available and there are uncertainties on the potential impact on growth and tooth development, which require regular monitoring.

Regarding safety, the side effects associated with Ofev were considered manageable with dose interruptions or reductions.""" .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:ce99ebb1-2851-47b3-bf8f-780bc9979eb6> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:5156eef8-6fc1-4b91-b330-9e3cfaa52b70> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 3 ;
    kg:section_id "ce99ebb1-2851-47b3-bf8f-780bc9979eb6" ;
    kg:section_title "1.1  Idiopathic Pulmonary Fibrosis" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text "OFEV is indicated for the treatment of adults with idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis (IPF)." .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:d02488c4-6e6b-4e92-8028-b5a0d3304adb> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:c8633e11-c806-45b0-9dbe-52af82db8b21> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 13 ;
    kg:section_id "d02488c4-6e6b-4e92-8028-b5a0d3304adb" ;
    kg:section_title "8.6  Hepatic Impairment" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text "Nintedanib is predominantly eliminated via biliary/fecal excretion (greater than 90%). In a PK study performed in patients with hepatic impairment (Child Pugh A, Child Pugh B), exposure to nintedanib was increased [see Clinical Pharmacology (12.3)] . In patients with mild hepatic impairment (Child Pugh A), the recommended dosage of OFEV is 100 mg twice daily [see Dosage and Administration (2.3)] . Monitor for adverse reactions and consider treatment interruption, or discontinuation for management of adverse reactions in these patients [see Dosage and Administration (2.4)]. Treatment of patients with moderate (Child Pugh B) and severe (Child Pugh C) hepatic impairment with OFEV is not recommended [see Warnings and Precautions (5.1)]." .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:d2d3fed3-3838-425a-af8a-118326fe3ab8> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:b8fd6ff0-a9a9-44aa-ab2c-052e40e004f3> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 7 ;
    kg:section_id "d2d3fed3-3838-425a-af8a-118326fe3ab8" ;
    kg:section_title "6.1  Clinical Trials Experience" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "OFEV_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text """Because clinical trials are conducted under widely varying conditions, adverse reaction rates observed in the clinical trials of a drug cannot be directly compared to rates in the clinical trials of another drug and may not reflect the rates observed in practice.

The safety of OFEV was evaluated in over 1000 IPF patients, 332 patients with chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype, and over 280 patients with SSc-ILD. Over 200 IPF patients were exposed to OFEV for more than 2 years in clinical trials.""" .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:dc466117-741b-4411-a8c6-0893e6dd88bc> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "ofev-epar-medicines-overview_en.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:ofev:chunk:b8694e1f-60ff-4cd0-9c61-96e111b258b5> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 3 ;
    kg:section_id "dc466117-741b-4411-a8c6-0893e6dd88bc" ;
    kg:section_title "What measures are being taken to ensure the safe and effective use of Ofev?" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "dcf1cfdd-57dc-4936-b9b2-0839e9684cb2" ;
    kg:source_document_type "product_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "ofev-epar-medicines-overview_en.pdf" ;
    kg:text """Recommendations and precautions to be followed by healthcare professionals and patients for the safe and effective use of Ofev have been included in the summary of product characteristics and the package leaflet.

As for all medicines, data on the use of Ofev are continuously monitored. Side effects reported with Ofev are carefully evaluated and any necessary action taken to protect patients.""" .

<urn:kg:ofev:section:e13195d5-70eb-4b93-bfa9-788e7dd45818> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf" ;
